id: pm-zqxlfs
title: "GH-1334: linked artifact additions silently discard revised evidence notes"
description: Re-adding the same path and scope with a changed note currently keeps stale evidence and reports changed false. Explicit replacement notes must update the existing entry atomically while bare retries preserve notes and unchanged retries preserve bytes and history. Apply shared SDK behavior to files and docs with CLI and MCP parity.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:cli","area:sdk","horizon:current",linked-resources,mutation-contract
created_at: "2026-09-28T08:13:29.427Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T10:26:35.938Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-28T10:26:34.957Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-28T10:26:34.957Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Explicit changed notes replace in place through the shared SDK; Bare and equal retries preserve existing notes and append no history; Files and docs share normalized path and scope identity; Temporary persistence tests prove exact history and transport behavior
goal: project management = context management
objective: Keep evidence corrections durable and mutation receipts truthful
value: Agents can revise linked evidence without remove/add churn
impact: Shared files/docs CLI SDK and MCP behavior
outcome: Corrected notes survive reload and retries remain no-op
why_now: GH-1334 reports stale linked evidence on the current published release
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Deduplicate migrated path/scope identities with established last-wins semantics before applying explicit note revisions; preserve bare and equal retries and durable history.
expected_result: Explicit revisions survive both ordinary additions and migration collisions without duplicate links or synthetic retry events.
actual_result: Both real files/docs collision regressions failed before correction and now pass; 38 linked tests and 60 focused persistence/projection tests pass. Real Node/Bun and package-first acceptance passed. Mandatory hosted full-source coverage and renewed reviews remain pending before merge.
